note {'text': '**By Claude Code** — **Correction (2026-11-26):** my earlier note repeated commit 635edd03\'s explanation, "several webcams and none marked primary". Production data does not support it. Both agents always mark exactly one webcam primary. Of the two affected printers (both moonraker-obico 2.0.9), one currently reports an empty webcam list and the other one primary webcam with an empty name. moonraker-obico reports an empty list when every webcam has streaming disabled, or when starting the stream fails with any error other than "Janus not found" (`webcam_stream.py`: `normalized_webcams` stays `[]`). So the real state is "this printer has no streamable webcam right now", and it is a normal state. The crash needs one more condition: the person once saved a rotation for this printer, while it still had a webcam.\n**Where the fix belongs:** the app copies the same "find the primary webcam, then read its rotation" code into four screens (PrinterItem, PrinterCard, PrinterControls, FullScreenWebCam). 635edd03 fixed only one of them. The fix (proposal, not made) is one shared hook that returns no webcam and no rotation when the list is empty, used by all four. The second printer\'s crash at 03:22 UTC is not explained by its current data; a hypothesis (not verified) is that its stream had failed at that moment, so its list was briefly empty.'}
