e895b0d065 Failures go to whoever can act on them: system refusals of a save or an export, a refused printer key and a deactivated account to the person; a too-long chat and a broken AI panel to us
- Saving: a refusal from the system (permission denied, operation not permitted, read-only, disk
  full, on a path inside the project folder) is thrown as Workspace::SaveRefused, carrying the
  folder and the system's reason, from whichever autosave call met it. Each caller catches it
  once: File > Save, dropping setting changes and a restart show it titled "Couldn't save";
  export, restore and open show it in their own dialog; an AI tool call returns `refused`.
  Autosave's own retries show it once, until a save works again. It is not reported. Any other
  save failure is ours: autosave reports it once when saving goes from working to failing, and a
  successful save ends that run of failures. Kenneth: "tell the main session to implement this
  design".
- The project store writes its small files (HEAD, pins, current state, operations, manifests)
  through the C library and throws std::filesystem::filesystem_error with the system's code, so
  a full disk or a read-only project folder is the person's and not reported as ours.
- A restart from Preferences whose save the system refuses says why and does not restart.
- Opening a project held by another JusPrin window says so. Kenneth: "Yes".
- Export, restore and version history show the system's words when it refuses, and report
  anything else. Export accepts ".3MF".
- An AI tool call whose save the system refuses, or whose export folder it refuses, returns the
  `refused` code with the system's reason and is not reported.
- The Home card says "Moonraker at <address> refused the app's key. Press Reconnect to enter it."
  on a 401 or 403. Kenneth: "Yes".
- A chat too long for the model is ours: its own sentence is removed and the error goes to the
  top handler with the service's status, request id and text.
- The AI panel's four start-up failures are reported once; Retry does not report again.
- Credits and plans, Billing and usage and Delete account tell no answer (internet sentence),
  401 (sign in again), 426 (update) and any other answer (ours, reported) apart.
- A deactivated account's email code or password sign-in says "This account has been
  deactivated. If you think this is a mistake, email jusprin-support@obico.io." Kenneth: "do it
  this way".
- Automatic reports drop a repeat of a failure already sent in this run, as the dialog already
  did. Kenneth: "go with your pick".

