lastActive":"2026-11-28T14:28:58.503179Z","isSuperuser":true,"isStaff":true,"experiments":{},"emails":[{"id":"12","email":"k@obico.io","is_verified":true}],"options":{"theme":"light","language":"en","stacktraceOrder":-1,"timezone":"America/Los_Angeles","clock24Hours":false},"flags":{"newsletter_consent_prompt":false},"avatar":{"avatarType":"letter_avatar","avatarUuid":null},"identities":[]},"type":"note","data":{"text":"**By Claude Code** — Fixed in obico-server master acb28b11 (pushed 2026-11-28, not yet in a release). The cause: `POST /api/v1/octo/printer_events/` called `.lower()` on `notify`, which only works on the plugins' form data ('t'/'f'). A user's own Python script, signed in with their printer's auth token, sent JSON with `notify: true`, exactly as the API doc describes, and got a 500. The view now converts `notify` to text first, so JSON true/false and form 't'/'f' both work. Reproduced locally before the fix; new test PrinterEventPostTestCase covers both forms; all 130 api tests pass. Resolved in the next release. The neighbouring crash on a missing event_text (OBICO-SERVER-B2A) is unchanged and stays ignored."},"dateCreated":"2026-11-28T14:32:00.081300Z"},{"id":"3091","user":{"id":"1","name":"k@obico.io","username":"k@obico.io","email":"k@obico.io","avatarUrl":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d5e6802ffc3ff5b8c67e2c09916068e1?s=32&d=mm","isActive":true,"hasPasswordAuth":true,"isManaged":false,"dateJoined":"2020-01-09T04:53:47.989443Z","lastLogin":"2026-11-24T19:15:21.724717Z","has2fa":false,"lastActive":"2026-11-28T14:28:58.503179Z","isSuperuser":true,"isStaff":true,"experiments":{},"emails":[{"id":"12","email":"k@obico.io","is_verified":true}],"options":{"theme":"light","language":"en","stacktraceOrder":-1,"timezone":"America/Los_Angeles","clock24Hours":false},"flags":{"newsletter_consent_prompt":false},"avatar":{"avatarType":"letter_avatar","avatarUuid":null},"identities":[]},"type":"note","data":{"text":"**By Claude Code** — **Triage (2026-11-25):** A user (account 264108) posted to `/api/v1/octo/printer_events/` from their own Python script (`Python-urllib/3.13`), sending JSON with `"notify": true` and the title "System Health - JSON Push Test". `api/octoprint_views.py:413` does `request.data.get('notify', '').lower()`, which only works for the string the plugins send as form data; a JSON boolean raises AttributeError and the request returns 500.
**Why now:** Our code: lines 405-415 last changed 2024-05-27, nothing recent. Dependencies: not involved. Client/environment: a new client, a hand-written script calling the plugin API with JSON instead of the plugins' form data; account age not checked. Really new: yes, first event of this exact message; OBICO-SERVER-B2A (missing `event_text`, `.replace` on None) is the same line family with a different field.
**Impact:** 1 event, 1 user, only their custom script; real plugins are not affected.
**Classification:** needs attention (low priority). Suggested fix: `str(request.data.get('notify', '')).lower() in ['t', 'true']` (accepts bool and string), and `(request.data.get('event_text') or '')` for B2A's case."},"dateCreated":"2026-11-26T00:33:06.209549Z"},{"id":"0","user":null,"type":"first_seen","data":{},"dateCreated":"2026-11-25T22:20:30.655314Z"}]}
